# Values here are duplicated from _data/author.yml because GitHub parses this file
# directly and cannot read Jekyll data. Change both together.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this framework, please cite it.
title: "How Regulatory Order Reaches Actors: A Three-Module Framework"
abstract: >-
  A framework for tracing how regulatory order forms and reaches actors across
  AI-related value chains. Two independent classification axes — Instability (conditions) and
  Formation History (events) — plus a downstream module describing transmission,
  distribution, and re-formation once an order exists.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lim
    given-names: Gaeun
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-1332-9206"
    affiliation: Independent researcher
version: "4.0"
date-released: 2026-08-18
license: CC-BY-4.0
url: "https://gaeunlim01.github.io/regulatory-order/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/GaeunLim01/regulatory-order"
keywords:
  - regulatory analysis
  - export control
  - AI governance
  - semiconductors
  - value chains


---
layout: default
title: Overview
description: Five layers for tracing how regulatory order forms and reaches actors across AI-related value chains.
---

<section class="hero" id="overview">
  <div class="shell">
    <span class="eyebrow">Framework v5</span>
    <h1>How regulatory order reaches actors</h1>
    <p class="standfirst">One methodology, five layers. One library of real cases tagged against it.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tight">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="axes axes--one">
      <a class="axis" href="{{ '/method/' | relative_url }}">
        <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--accent">Methodology</span>
        <p class="axis__q">How does regulatory order form, and how does it reach the actors standing under it?</p>
      </a>
    </div>
    <ul class="axes-note layer-index">
      <li><span>A</span> Classification: why is the object unstable</li>
      <li><span>B</span> Formation: how the boundary reached its current shape</li>
      <li><span>C</span> Manifestation: how it shows up in the record</li>
      <li><span>D</span> Distribution: who ends up holding it</li>
      <li><span>E</span> Re-formation: what happens next</li>
    </ul>

    <a class="spotlight" href="{{ '/cases/' | relative_url }}">
      <span class="eyebrow">Case library</span>
      <p class="spotlight__q">Real disputes, tagged against all five layers at once.</p>
      <p class="spotlight__cases">Super Micro · Anthropic v. DoW · Fable 5 · RASA · EU AI Act</p>
    </a>
  </div>
</section>

